course: dictionary
lesson: 2405
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The easiest way to choose the right one is to read the words around it, which is its context. «Custom» is a good example because it has four meanings, and the sentence tells you which one you need.
explain: «In the UK people value queuing very highly, and jumping the queue makes them upset; knowing such customs helps you avoid offending anyone.» Here a custom is a way of behaving that a whole group of people follows. The clue is «people value queuing». Try your meaning in the sentence: "knowing such ways of doing things helps you avoid offending anyone" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Look at the words next to it, too. «Go through customs» at an airport means passing the check at the border. «Custom-made» means made specially for one person. Small words like «local», «old» or «made» often show you which meaning is needed.
fact: A custom is a way of doing something that people in a place or group have done for a long time.
fact: A custom can also be a habit of one person, such as going for a walk after dinner.
fact: «Customs» can mean the place at an airport or border where officers check what people bring into a country.
fact: «Custom-made» means made specially for one person.
fact: It is a custom to say «Happy Diwali» or «Eid Mubarak» to friends who celebrate, and being curious and kind about other customs is good manners.
exercise: «To introduce a friend to an older person, the old custom is to say the older person's name first.» What is a custom in this sentence? | A place where officers check bags | *A way people have done something for a long time | A coat made for one person | A loud noise at a party
exercise: «After the long flight, Sam had to go through customs before he could collect his bag.» Where did Sam go through customs? | A row of seats on the plane | *The airport check where officers look at what people bring in | A shop that sells old clothes | A party where everyone sings
exercise: «It was his custom to walk after dinner.» What does custom mean here? | A type of supper | A kind of warm coat | A law for the whole country | *A habit of one person
test: «Her bike was custom-made, so no one else had one just like it.» What does custom-made mean? | *Made specially for one person | Very old and rusty | Made in a factory with many other bikes | Stolen from a shop
test: «It is a custom to give presents at Christmas.» Which meaning of custom is this? | Something made just for one person | The check at a border | A habit of one person | *A way of doing something that many people have done for a long time
exam: Which phrase means a check at an airport or border? | *Go through customs | Custom-made | Old custom | Local custom
